From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme, user32: paint Luna frames and theme parts with fewer blits

Purpose: let the XP shell's windows (Luna) and the bridge's frames resize
smoothly, also in virtual machines without a GPU.
Wine before (with 0069-0069): each step of a resize painted the frame
twice: on WM_NCPAINT, then all of it again when 0070 updated the caption
region on WM_WINDOWPOSCHANGED. DefWindowProc drew the classic caption, with
themed buttons, under the Luna caption that covered it right after. Every
blit of an 8- or 24-bpp theme image converted it to the screen's 32 bpp,
colour-keyed parts went through TransparentBlt (two memory DCs, two
bitmaps and five blits each), and the shaped windows' subclass asked
wineserver for its window property at every message.
Change:
- Theme images of fewer than 32 bpp are kept as 32-bpp copies holding the
  bytes that converting them for a 32-bpp target gives (fourth byte zero);
  their default transparent colour is found before.
- For a window's DC on a 32-bpp screen without a mapping, 0073's resized
  colour-keyed parts are drawn with AlphaBlend from a copy whose key pixels
  have alpha 0 and the others 255, which leaves the same pixels as
  TransparentBlt there.
- A WM_WINDOWPOSCHANGED that only resizes updates the caption region
  without painting; the part that the new region uncovers is painted at
  once (RDW_ERASENOW) instead of later.
- user32's DefWindowProc leaves the band that the Luna caption covers
  (new Win4WineCaptionBand) out of the update region of the classic
  WM_NCPAINT, which then skips its caption; the menu bar and the borders
  below are painted as before.
- The shaped windows are found in a list of the process instead of a
  window property.
Evidence: 13 scenes of the English XP session (Luna) on Xvfb are identical
pixel for pixel with and without the patch: the desktop, Notepad and
Mousepad's frame active and inactive, the Start menu, My Computer moved, a
menu, Notepad maximized, restored, made smaller and larger, Mousepad made
smaller and larger. Dragging the bottom-right corner 100 steps of 16 ms on
Xvfb (with 0039): Mousepad's frame took 71-99 sizes growing and all 100
shrinking (38-51 and 55 before), Notepad 71-75 and 87-94 (28-29 and
39-41). In the test VM (QEMU, standard VGA), of 80 steps: Mousepad 68-72
and 72-77 (40-41 and 42-46), My Computer 29-33 (18-20).
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL and a visual style; classic frames
are unchanged.
